I've been playing a wizard who has been coming along rather nicely.  I've
encountered some situations that I don't know how to deal with yet, and would
like some pointers on what to do next.  Since my questions may be spoilers
for other players, I'll use the obligatory control-L to protect them.

Okay.  Here goes.

   1.  I have completed my quest and obtained the Bell of Opening, which I
       gather from other postings is supposed to be used at the bottom of
       the gnomish mines to gain access to something.  I've been to the 
       bottom of the mines and I think I know where this location is.  I've
       also gathered that I need a candleabra and a special book (seems like
       I recall something like this from the old Infocom classic, "Zork".), 
       neither of which I have yet.  I am back in the main dungeon (currently
       in the Valley of the Dead below the castle).  Have I missed these other
       two items or will they be found later?

   2.  While exploring the dungeon, I hit a trap door that dropped me from
       somewhere above the Medusa level to somewhere below the Medusa level.
       Since I wound up in a maze, I made sure I had a blindfold on when I
       ascended the stairs since I didn't know where I would encounter the
       Medusa.  I managed to survive the Medusa, but I now have another
       problem; I can't find a stairway *UP* from this level.  I have explored
       and searched everywhere and even tried a couple of unusual things like
       putting on a ring of levitation and trying to dig a hole in the ceiling.
       I've also magic mapped the level and still cannot find the way up.  The
       last time I descended this far, I got to the Medusa level via the
       stairs and I think there was a stairway up on this level, though I
       don't remember for sure.  I have a couple of things to try if there is
       in fact no stairway up; maybe a cursed scroll of teleporation (I have
       the teleport control intrinsic) or possibly a cursed potion of gain
       level.

   3.  What do you do with those pesky liches?  In this particular game I used
       a blessed scroll of genocide to eliminate them.  The last time I got 
       this far, I encountered a master lich that would not stay still long
       enough for me to kill it.  I tried standing on the up stairs so it could
       not escape up a level, but it just teleported all over the place.  My
       armor class was high enough that it couldn't really hurt me, but it was
       really irritating to have that stoopid thing teleport in for a quick
       exchange of blows while trying to eat, etc.

That ought to be enough for now.  I would appreciate any suggestions or hints
that anyone could offer.  Thanks.

